		(descr "Peltier module 20 x 20 mm (TES1-4902) on an exposed copper pad; both leads leave one edge (towards the slot) at its corners, onto pads just past it: pad 1 at -x, pad 2 at +x. Fit all six the same way up, so the same lead colour lands on pad 1 everywhere Hand-soldered variant (lid_2, 2026-10-08): no stencil paste on the hand-soldered pads, which keep other copper 0.45 mm off (so traces near them stay under a wide mask dam). The module pad's mask opening sits 0.15 mm inside its copper: traces beside it keep a >= 0.2 mm mask dam after the fab's own expansion; the pad stays bare for thermal paste.")
